sts and a lot more  twice as many tests available now than  before the pandemic a large proportion  of those i've only been able to do  because we're no longer actually in the  eu okay how are you feeling about civil  servants working from home um london  tech week conference uh yesterday sarah  healey um said that she enjoys working  from home she's a top mandarin so she  because she can spend more time on her  peloton exercise bike  well look i think we're in a world now  um where people where there is a  combination people were working from  home people are going into the office i  i had a look actually i know some the  last week for which i have numbers there  are about 1  300  uh transport official  civil servants in the  in the office i i i've been in this  weekend people are pleased to to come  back to the office there will be times  when people want to work from home we  are in this sort of transition um stage  through the uh through the autumn um and  uh and i i think things will settle down  into uh probably more of a hybrid world  but there's nothing like the spark of  being in the office um as as a lot of my  team found this this last week or two  although you find it very productive  being working from home don't you  minister can never get you in here can  we i'd be loving love to come and see  you  when when when when when oh well  as soon as you invite me on again okay  i'd like to okay we'll see you next week  i do find genuinely um that it's helpful  to be in the office there are times  where uh it's quite nice to be at home  when you're um on the radio first thing  okay um and on the tele box uh talk to  me about lateral flow test before i let  you go and there were some suggestions  that the pcrs would be replaced by  lateral flow tests when in time for  uh half term holidays for the kids i was  reading yesterday that there aren't  enough lateral flow tests and there  aren't enough people who will be able to  supervise those lateral flow tests via  zoom or whatever and so that's not going  to happen is that wrong  i don't think that's right this is my  colleagues over at the department of  health have been working very hard on  this and i know they've got the the date  of half term uh in mind  we did need to give the  producers of these things some time  because of course they've been busily  producing pcr tests over the summer um  to switch production to lateral flow um  but uh it looks to me like uh like  they'll be able to step up to that i  noticed actually in ireland um yesterday  uh that little came along with a pack of  uh which they're selling in their stores  in in in the republic there for 25 euros  and you get five lateral flow tests uh i  uh you know look forward to the  expansion of a lateral flow test perhaps  into supermarkets and elsewhere um as we  as we get on to the point where people  can buy those for returning from holiday  so you think a little uh lateral flow  test should be accepted as um currency  enough or does it have to be a little  bit more formal than that  well it will be for the department of  health to to set out the rules about how  people need to go about this but  remember with pcr tests uh you didn't  have to be  supervised as it were you had to get  that pcr test in advance you had to  record the fact that you ordered it uh  but you were then trusted to get on and  do it obviously the department of health  will put some guidance in place as to  how they want this to operate and  they're still working on that so i won't  tread on their toes but i i've every  confidence that the system will be gone  up and running uh in good time  but you're still uh hopeful that the  lateral flow  ruling will be in place for the  half-term holidays i i am as i say  they're working on the detail of this  and the the private market is having to  respond to  uh that shift to using lateral flows and  of course they need hundreds of  thousands even millions of them  available so and there's 